\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Remember all the people
\par Who lives in far-off lands,
\par In strange and lovely cities,
\par Or roam the desert sands,
\par Or farm the mountain pastures,
\par Or till the endless plains
\par Where children wade through ricefields
\par And watch the camel-trains:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Some work in sultry forests
\par Where apes swing to and fro,
\par Some fish in mighty rivers,
\par Some hunt across the snow.
\par Remember all God's children,
\par Who yet have never heard
\par The truth that comes from Jesus,
\par The glory of His word.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. God bless the men and women
\par Who serve Him oversea;
\par God raise up more to help them
\par To set the nations free,
\par Till all the distant people
\par In every foreign place
\par Shall understad His Kingdom
\par And come into His grace.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

